{"jurisdiction":"NE","generatedAt":"2026-11-05T05:54:04Z","bills":{"NE-2025-LR480":{"id":"NE-2025-LR480","passed":false,"number":"LR 480","title":"Interim study to examine how public resources for youth development programming are currently distributed across Nebraska, identify gaps in availability and access, particularly in rural areas and communities with fewer resources, and develop recommendations for ensuring those resources work more efficiently and effectively for youth, families, and communities","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-03-25","sponsor":{"name":"Bostar","party":"Nonpartisan","state":"NE","district":"29"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-09-21","text":"Notice of hearing for October 28, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-30","text":"Referred to Education Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-25","text":"Referred to Executive Board","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-25","text":"Date of introduction","chamber":"Legislature"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/bills/search_by_date.php?SessionDay=2026","textUrl":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR480.pdf","versions":[{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR480.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"This resolution would direct the Education Committee to study how public money for youth development programs is spread across Nebraska. It would look for gaps in access, especially in rural areas and other low-resource communities, and review ways to better coordinate funding and improve results for youth, families, and communities. The committee would then report its findings and recommendations to the Legislature or Legislative Council.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":fal